    "general_information": [
      {
        "type": "GeneralTitle",
        "content": "IMPORTANT MAJOR INFORMATION",
        "groupId": "b6ba6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
        "position": 0,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralText",
        "content": "<p>The Asian American Studies major promotes the study of the histories, contemporary realities, and diverse experiences of Asian and Pacific Islander Americans. The BA program in Asian American Studies provides a general introduction for students who anticipate advanced work at the graduate level or careers in research, public service, and community work related to Asian and Pacific Islander Americans.</p><p><br></p><p>Listed below are the lower division preparation courses for the major.</p><p><br></p><p>To be considered for this major, you must <strong><u>complete a minimum of one course from the required major preparatory section listed below</u></strong> by the end of spring before transfer:</p><ul><li>One lower division Asian American Studies course that focuses on Asian Americans or Ethnic Studies.</li></ul><p>All courses must be taken for a letter grade.</p><p><br></p><p>For more information regarding this major and UCLA's transfer selection process, visit <u style=\"color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\">https://</u><a href=\"http://www.asianam.ucla.edu/undergraduate-study\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">asianam.ucla.edu</a> and <u style=\"color: rgb(41, 98, 255);\">https://</u><a href=\"http://www.admission.ucla.edu.\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">admission.ucla.edu.</a></p><p><br></p><p>PLEASE NOTE: the community college courses listed below have been approved to satisfy preparation for this major at UCLA, but they may not be exact equivalents of the UCLA courses listed.</p>",
        "groupId": "c2ba6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
        "position": 1,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralTitle",
        "content": "Additional NOTE",
        "groupId": "c0ba6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
        "position": 2,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralText",
        "content": "Important Note: Students should save all syllabi for all Asian American studies courses to petition the department for exemption from lower division requirements after admission.",
        "groupId": "baba6f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
        "position": 3,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralTitle",
        "content": "AP/IB CREDIT",
        "groupId": "daac2d06-61db-4d98-97cd-019a796c09ca",
        "position": 4,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralText",
        "content": "<p>No AP or IB exams are considered equivalent, and credit earned from those exams cannot be used towards the Asian American Studies major prep.</p>",
        "groupId": "2aa63797-9b97-4a03-8db5-019a796c09ca",
        "position": 5,
        "area": "General"
      }
    ],
